
This package is a Go port of the ITU-R P.533-14 HF circuit performance
model (version 14.2 of the reference code, P.1239-3 foF2 variability, P.842
reliability prediction, P.1240 operational MUF), developed by ITU-R Study
Group 3, Working Party 3L, https://www.itu.int/en/ITU-R/study-groups/rsg3/
(the P533 and ITURHFProp software of the ITU-R HF propagation package).

The ITURHFProp, P533 and P372 software has been developed collaboratively by
participants in ITU-R Study Group 3. It may be used by implementers in their
implementation of the Recommendation as well as in revisions of the specific
original Recommendation and in other ITU Recommendations, free from any
copyright assertions.

Modifications (2026-10, Luca IU2FRL):
  - Translated from C to Go, one Go file per original source file
    (P533.h is p533.go, Common.h is common.go, P533.c is p533_run.go,
    MedianAvailableReceiverPower.c is median_available_receiver_power.go, ...).
  - The model state is a pathData value (PathData), the calculation keeps the
    flow and the floating point operation order of the C code.
  - The tables of the C sources (absorption, Lh, normal distribution) were
    converted mechanically from the C initialisers.
  - ReadIonParameters.c, ReadP1239.c and ReadType13.c are ported without the
    text map reader (ReadIonParametersTxt). ReadAntennaPatterns.c of the
    ITURHFProp driver is ported as readAntennaFile (types 11, 13 and 14).
  - The P.372 noise model is the sub-package p372.
  - Memory allocation (PathMemory.c) and the diagnostic dump (InputDump.c,
    DumpPathData.c) have no counterpart; the C driver report is replaced by
    the Result type.
  - Return codes are mapped to Go error values.
  - Out-of-range antenna pattern indices (negative elevation angles), where
    the C code reads out of bounds, are clamped.

